.Dd September 30, 2026
.Dt PKG.CONF 5
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm pkg.conf
.Nd where this machine gets software from
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Pa /etc/novi/pkg.conf
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
tells
.Xr pkg 1
which mirror to fetch from and which key to believe.
Each line is
.Ar name No = Ar value ;
.Ql #
starts a comment.
.Pp
It is deliberately
.Em not
part of
.Xr system.conf 5 .
That file is the declared state of the machine, converged by
.Nm novi-state apply ;
this is a bootstrap parameter, and
.Xr novi-state 1
cannot install a package from a mirror it would have to read out of
the file it is in the middle of applying.
.Ss Settings
.Bl -tag -width "allow_unsigned"
.It Va mirror
A URL, or a local directory.
The installation medium carries the whole signed repository, so a
live system can install the desktop with no network at all.
The same verification runs either way; only the transport differs.
.Pp
The shipped value is
.Pa /run/live/novi-repo ,
which is the medium.
On an installed machine that path does not exist, and
.Xr novi-install 1
comments the line out unless it was given
.Fl -mirror :
there is no public Novi repository yet, and pointing a package
manager at a host that does not exist is worse than pointing it at
nothing.
.It Va key
The Ed25519 public key the index is verified with.
.Pp
This key must reach the machine by
.Sy some path other than the mirror it is used to check .
.Nm build/50-repo.sh
installs a development key into the image at build time, which is the
right answer when you built both.
.It Va allow_unsigned
.Cm no
by default.
.Cm yes
turns off signature checking entirely.
It exists for bootstrapping a repository you are in the middle of
creating.
On a machine you care about it means
.Dq run whatever the network hands me, as root .
.It Va allow_stale
.Cm no
by default.
The index carries a
.Va valid-until
.Em inside the signed blob ,
checked after the signature.
A signature says
.Dq this is genuine ;
it does not say
.Dq this is current .
Without an expiry, someone who can serve an old but validly signed
index \(em a hostile mirror, a captive portal, a stale cache \(em can
hold this machine at a version with a known hole indefinitely, with
every signature and every hash still checking out.
.Pp
.Nm pkg sync
refuses a stale index;
.Nm pkg update
only warns, because a machine that has been offline for a month
should explain why it has nothing to offer rather than stop working.
.Pp
If this machine has no battery-backed clock, fix the clock rather
than setting this: a wrong clock breaks the check in both directions.
.It Va timeout
Seconds a fetch may go with
.Sy nothing arriving
before
.Xr pkg 1
gives up.
Default 30.
.Pp
A
.Em read
timeout, not a total one, so a slow but progressing download of a
90 MB toolchain package is unaffected.
It has a value here because BusyBox
wget(1)'s
own default is 900 seconds, and that stopped being somebody else's
problem when
.Va packages.\& Ns Ar name No = Cm present
became something boot convergence converges: an unreachable mirror
would otherwise stall the boot for a quarter of an hour per declared
package, with nothing on the console to say why.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width "/var/cache/pkg/archives" -compact
.It Pa /etc/novi/pkg.conf
This file.
Base content, not owned by any package, because
.Xr pkg 1
overwrites a package's files on upgrade and this one exists to be
edited.
.It Pa /etc/novi/keys/novi-repo.pub
The default key.
.It Pa /var/cache/pkg/archives
Downloaded packages.
Every archive here is re-hashed against the signed index before it is
unpacked.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
Point at a repository you built and served yourself:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
mirror = https://packages.example.org/novi/x86_64
key    = /etc/novi/keys/novi-repo.pub
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr novi-install 1 ,
.Xr novi-verify 1 ,
.Xr pkg 1 ,
.Xr system.conf 5
.Sh STANDARDS
RFC 0006, RFC 0010.
